# Trivy suppression file.
#
# One entry per line. Formats:
#   CVE-2024-12345                       (silence a CVE globally)
#   CVE-2024-12345 exp:2026-01-01        (silence with expiry)
#   AVD-DS-0002                          (silence a misconfig rule id)
#
# Every entry should be justified in a comment. Prefer fixing over ignoring.

# KSV-0109 -- "ConfigMap stores secrets".
#
# Fires on rendered/all.yaml for rhdh-developer-hub-app-config, on the keys
# clientSecret, secret, password and token. Every one of those holds a shell
# placeholder, not a value:
#
#   clientSecret: ${AUTH_GITHUB_CLIENT_SECRET}
#   secret:       ${BACKEND_SECRET}
#   password:     ${POSTGRESQL_ADMIN_PASSWORD}
#   token:        ${GITHUB_TOKEN}
#
# RHDH expands these at boot from env vars sourced out of Secrets, which is the
# configuration mechanism the product documents -- there is no secret in the
# ConfigMap to move. Trivy matches on key name and cannot see the indirection.
# Re-check if app-config ever gains a key holding a literal.
AVD-KSV-0109
